1) Brand Snapshot (for the editor’s global context)

Brand promise

Elysian Leaders helps ambitious professionals build sustainable high-ticket online businesses that create time + financial freedom—with proven systems and real-world results, not hype.  ￼

Brand personality

Relatable luxury: premium, clean, elevated, approachable. Aspirational but never pretentious; grounded but never dull.  ￼

Brand principles (must be expressed in layout + copy)
	1.	Empowering
	2.	Authentic
	3.	Aspirational
	4.	Action-oriented  ￼

⸻

2) Audience + Desired Emotional Outcome

Primary audience

Ambitious professionals who want out of corporate constraints and into freedom—skeptical of “guru” hype; motivated by structure, sustainability, and credibility.  ￼

Emotional targets to hit on every page
	•	“This is real.” (credibility)
	•	“This is for me.” (belonging + relatability)
	•	“I can do this.” (empowerment)
	•	“I know what to do next.” (action)

⸻

3) Voice & Copy Rules (non-negotiables)

Voice guardrails

Conversational yet authoritative; confident not aggressive; inspiring not preachy; personal but professional.  ￼

Writing rules
	•	Empowering without hype (no “overnight success,” no unrealistic promises).  ￼
	•	Clarity over cleverness (plain language, no buzzword soup).  ￼
	•	Conversational authority (human cadence + substance).  ￼
	•	Aspirational realism (show what’s possible + what it takes).  ￼

Approved language bank

Use often: impact, purpose, alignment; wealth/abundance/fulfillment; freedom (time + financial); sustainable/long-term; build/create/design.  ￼

Avoid list

Hustle-culture language; get-rich-quick implications; corporate jargon; overly salesy urgency.  ￼

Taglines (use for hero, CTA, headers)

Primary: Build the business. Live the life.  ￼
Alt: Your freedom starts here / High-ticket systems. Real-world results / Design your income. Reclaim your time  ￼

⸻

4) Messaging Architecture (Content Pillars → Page Angles)

Every landing page must anchor to one primary pillar and optionally support with a secondary.
	1.	Freedom Architecture (systems, leverage, scalable acquisition)  ￼
	2.	Life Reclamation (exit the 9–5, reclaim time/relationships)  ￼
	3.	Proven Pathways (frameworks, transparency, case studies)  ￼
	4.	Sustainable Abundance (wealth + values + health + longevity)  ￼

