7) Landing Page Structure Templates

Pick the structure based on offer type. The editor should generate sections in this order.

Template A: “Lead Magnet / Free Audit / Free Training” (most common)
	1.	Hero (promise + primary CTA)
	2.	Social proof bar (logos/testimonials/metrics)
	3.	Problem agitation (without doom)
	4.	Solution overview (what they get)
	5.	How it works (3 steps)
	6.	Benefits (life + business outcomes)
	7.	What’s included (deliverables list)
	8.	Proof (case study or results snapshot)
	9.	FAQ (objection handling)
	10.	Final CTA (simple, action-forward)

Template B: “High-Ticket Program / Application”
	1.	Hero (identity + transformation)
	2.	Credibility (why trust)
	3.	Who it’s for / not for
	4.	The framework (pillars/steps)
	5.	What you get (modules, support, assets)
	6.	Proof (testimonials, before/after)
	7.	Offer details (timeline, commitment, investment framing)
	8.	FAQ
	9.	Application CTA + reassurance

Template C: “Webinar / Event”
	1.	Hero (topic + outcomes + date/time + CTA)
	2.	What you’ll learn (bullets)
	3.	Host credibility
	4.	For who / not for who
	5.	Agenda (3–5 items)
	6.	Testimonials
	7.	FAQ
	8.	Final CTA (register)

