8) Section-by-Section Component Specs (AI editor rules)

8.1 Hero Section (non-negotiable)

Goal: immediate clarity + credibility + desire + one action.

Hero layout options
	•	White background with turquoise accents OR
	•	Full turquoise background with white H1 + gold underline/accent bar  ￼

Hero must include
	•	H1: Transformation statement (realistic + compelling)
	•	Subhead: who it’s for + how it works (1–2 sentences)
	•	Primary CTA button (turquoise or gold gradient)
	•	Secondary CTA (text link): “See how it works” / “What’s included”
	•	Supporting credibility line: “proven systems,” “real-world results,” etc.  ￼

Hero CTA examples (brand-safe)
	•	Get the free audit
	•	Book your strategy call
	•	Watch the training
	•	Start here
(avoid: “Get rich now,” “Instantly,” “Guaranteed,” etc.)  ￼

⸻

8.2 Social Proof Bar

Goal: “This is legit.”

Approved proof types:
	•	Short testimonials (1–2 sentences)
	•	Metrics (if real)
	•	Simple logo row (if you have permission)
Design:
	•	White or cream background
	•	Gold accents for numbers; navy for labels  ￼

⸻

8.3 Problem Section (Agitate without negativity)

Goal: reflect their reality; don’t shame them.

Copy tone:
	•	empathetic, validating, calm
	•	avoid fear-mongering
Use framing:
	•	“If you’re great at what you do, but…”
	•	“If the 9–5 is starting to feel…” (brand examples include this style)  ￼

⸻

8.4 Solution Overview

Goal: what the offer is in plain terms.

Structure:
	•	3–5 bullets or cards
	•	Each item: outcome first → mechanism second
Design:
	•	Card grid with rounded corners
	•	Turquoise headings; gold icons/numbers

⸻

8.5 How It Works (3 steps)

Goal: “I can see the path.”

Format:
	•	Step 1: Clarify / Align
	•	Step 2: Build / Implement
	•	Step 3: Launch / Optimize
(Adjust verbs per offer; keep parallel structure.)  ￼

Design:
	•	Big gold step numbers; navy text; optional turquoise header bar style (slide-inspired)  ￼

⸻

8.6 Benefits (Life + Business)

Goal: blend aspiration + realism.

Two-column pattern:
	•	Business outcomes (revenue, clarity, acquisition system)
	•	Life outcomes (time, flexibility, presence, fulfillment)  ￼

⸻

8.7 What’s Included (Deliverables)

Goal: tangible value.

Format options:
	•	Checklist cards (best)
	•	Icon list (minimal)
Rules:
	•	Keep it scannable
	•	Avoid long paragraphs
	•	“Premium but approachable” packaging language

⸻

8.8 Proof Section (Case Study / Results Snapshot)

Goal: convert skepticism into belief.

Use one of:
	•	Before/after narrative
	•	“What changed” bullets
	•	Stats slide style (huge gold number + context)  ￼

Tone:
	•	transparent, grounded, no exaggerated claims  ￼

⸻

8.9 FAQ (Objection Handling)

Goal: remove friction.

Include:
	•	Time commitment
	•	“What if I’m starting from scratch?”
	•	“Who is this for / not for?”
	•	Support/implementation details
	•	“How soon will I see results?” (answer realistically)

⸻

8.10 Final CTA Section (Singular focus)

Design:
	•	Full turquoise background
	•	White headline (“Your Next Step” style)
	•	Gold gradient CTA block/button  ￼

Copy:
	•	short, confident, action-forward
	•	reassure: “simple next step,” “no pressure,” etc.

